<title>HUNGARY: ICH PAYS PURCHASE PRICE FOR HUNGARY FORUM HOTEL.</title>
<headline>ICH PAYS PURCHASE PRICE FOR HUNGARY FORUM HOTEL.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese-owned Inter-Continental Hotels Corp (ICH) paid the $49.4 million purchase price for Hungary's four-star hotel Forum Szalloda Rt, Hungary's state privatisation agency APV said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;In line with the sale agreement signed on October 4, Inter-Continental fulfilled its payment obligations for $49.4 million and from November 1 became the owner of a 94.91 percent stake in Forum Szalloda Rt,&quot; APV said in a statement.</p>
<p>ICH will invest more than $11 million within three years to upgrade the Forum to five stars and will eventually change the name to the Hotel Inter-Continental Budapest.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
